message: "If you use Lockin, please cite it as below. It helps the project get credit."
title: "Lockin: strict focus commitment for Android"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ahmadrrrtx"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ahmadrrrtx/lockin"
url: "https://github.com/ahmadrrrtx/lockin"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-30
keywords:
  - android
  - focus
  - productivity
  - accessibility
  - privacy
  - offline-first
  - app-blocking
abstract: >-
  Lockin is an open-source, offline-first Android application for strict
  focus commitment. The user selects installed applications and a duration;
  once a session is committed, the state machine enforces ACTIVE until the
  deadline with no cancellation, pause, or early-unlock surface on any
  notification, broadcast, or interface. Blocking is implemented with a
  minimized accessibility service, sessions survive process death and reboot,
  and the app declares no INTERNET permission.
